style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo11;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>M1 is due to build next =
week.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo11;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We upgraded to gcc 13 after =
fixes for the major issues in OE-Core were =
found<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo11;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>New uninative releases were =
made to enable support on distros where they&#8217;re upgraded to gcc 13 =
versions.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo11;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The 5.15 kernel was dropped =
from master in preparation for adding a new kernel version later in the =
development cycle.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l13 =
level1 lfo12;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There is discussion about =
changing the CVE_CHECK_IGNORE functionality, please comment in the =
discussion on the list if you have opinions on what we should do =
there.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l13 =
level1 lfo12;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>FILE_LAYERNAME support was =
added to bitbake, paving the way for layer specific override =
support.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l13 =
level1 lfo12;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Autobuilder intermittent issues =
continue to be an issue. One set of intermittent issues was tracked down =
in glib tests and a fix was accepted upstream but other issues =
remain.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l13 =
level1 lfo12;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A number of recent changes =
combined together to lower our overall patch count to the lowest =
we&#8217;re seen in years, it is great to see patches improving over =
time, albeit slowly!<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Ways to =
contribute:</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l1 level1 =
lfo13;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>As people are likely aware, the =
project has a number of components which are either unmaintained, or =
have people with little to no time trying to keep them alive. These =
components include: patchtest, layerindex, devtool, toaster, wic, oeqa, =
autobuilder, CROPs containers, pseudo and more. Many have open bugs. =
Help is welcome in trying to better look after these =
components!<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
